{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 22, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 22, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=23&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=21&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 694562150, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r694562150-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Just filing amazing ", "text": "Tha pashipati is one of Nepal's largest religions sites and its is also very familiar on the world this temple is very old structure there are many sculptures worth seeing here I think those who will be visit here \n       You will be fascinated by this idols so you must visite this and one thing in Nepal  that's  reason I recommend that you get a lot to see here theology of Nepal's", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 38, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "51D0A3DBD8CBCE229454A4D62A48B080", "name": "Ramesh", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/501rameshn", "username": "501rameshn", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/18/c9/92/bc/avatar.jpg", "contribution_count": 127, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 311304, "location_name": "Sapa", "location_name_detailed": "Sapa, Vietnam"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-08-01", "published_at_date": "2019-08-01"}, {"review_id": 694180492, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r694180492-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A cultural must", "text": "This temple is filthy, dirty and smells of urine. Let's not forget these things. However, this is the first time I've seen open Hindu cremation, the full ritual, from washing the corpse to setting the pyre alight is in full view. It feels awkward and shocking to watch a stiff dead body being washed and then literally breathe in the smoke from the flames consuming it - but a unique insight into death within another culture. Definitely for these reasons, this temple is not suitable for young children.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E859443D57A8B0E9F8DC26A07E23C6A2", "name": "Jacob S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/jacobs624", "username": "jacobs624", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/c4/be/4b/jacob-s.jpg", "contribution_count": 191, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/18/92/2f/ab/funeral-pyres-along-the.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-07-30", "published_at_date": "2019-07-30"}, {"review_id": 693368421, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r693368421-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A place where one can reflect on life. What is life. one day everyone leaves so do your best to be happy", "text": "Lots of noise and people. beautiful temple. There are funeral pyre at the back of the temple. Its really humbling as there are people of all ages being cremated. Make one think that our time in earth is very limited so its so important to be happy and do what you want to do much as you can. Good place to just watch and relfect. i always go here every time i go to Nepal. Its one of the holiest temple for hindu but it does not matter what religion you are you can still see the temple from the back. There are also holy men. However the proper sadhu are away from the temple in the woods within pasupatinath.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4AE1C3314CF6A00A6628BA656C4D26D0", "name": "Watfordjohn", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/bakka11", "username": "bakka11", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e5/66/default-avatar-2020-53.jpg", "contribution_count": 44, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187058, "location_name": "Watford", "location_name_detailed": "Watford, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-07-28", "published_at_date": "2019-07-28"}, {"review_id": 693123420, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r693123420-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Amazing temple of Lord Shiva", "text": "Pashupati nath is one of the major attractions in Kathmandu. Had amazing architecture and you should atleast spare around an hour to visit it. There is a ghaat just besides the temple where the nepali cremation happens. Photography inside the temple is prohibited", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2019-07-31"}, "revi