i, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-07-14", "published_at_date": "2019-07-14"}, {"review_id": 689391743, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r689391743-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "One of the most sacred Hindu temples in Nepal", "text": "Had visited this Hindu temple in Kathmandu a long back ago. This temple is located on the banks of the Bagmati river and is a popular tourist attraction.\n\nThis Hindu temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva and is the oldest temple complex in Nepal. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and is a Hindu holiest shrine. It is visited by pilgrims from Nepal & India as well as foreign tourists. This temple complex has many smaller shrines, an ashram, small lingas, a cremation site near the river etc. There are some sages living in this temple. Mahashivratri is celebrated in this temple with great pomp & enthusiasm. Before entering the temple, footwear should be removed. Photography is allowed. Outside the temple, there are shops selling Rudraksha malas or necklaces. There is no entry fee for visiting the temple. The road leading to the temple is crowded, filthy and dirty.\n\nThis Hindu temple is an ideal place of worship for local devotees as well as people from other faith. It is a must visit and should not be missed while in Kathmandu.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9405F7CA3D154869BBDD87BBF43A3DB7", "name": "Cedric N", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/CedricN276", "username": "CedricN276", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ea/b2/default-avatar-2020-69.jpg", "contribution_count": 692, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554,